End a body that has neither Content-Length nor chunked encoding at the
end of the connection, as before FRP-6354. The retry support added there
treats every end of connection as a body cut short, so such a download,
such as the output of an httpd CGI program, was requested again and
again until the tries ran out, never reported as saved, and still exited
with status 0. A body that is shorter than its Content-Length or that
ends before its last chunk is still retried. Clear content_len on the
way out, since a redirect's Content-Length may be left in it.

---
 networking/wget.c |    5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/networking/wget.c
+++ b/networking/wget.c
@@ -1072,6 +1072,11 @@
 			 * fread does not distinguish between EOF and error.
 			 */
 			if (errno != EAGAIN) {
+				/* With no length and no chunks, EOF ends the body */
+				if (!G.got_clen && !ferror(dfp)) {
+					G.content_len = 0; /* may be left from a redirect */
+					break;
+				}
 				progress_meter(PROGRESS_END);
 				if (ferror(dfp)) {
 					bb_simple_perror_msg(bb_msg_read_error);
